  message: "DONE — same PR as WI-sirir (the mirror-image half of the same profile/schema disagreement).\n\nThe schema declared profile.total_files and profile.total_lines; a fresh self-survey confirms the producer emits NEITHER (profile keys are exactly dev_frameworks, framework_evidence, framework_mode, frameworks, languages).\n\nREMOVED rather than populated, on two grounds. (1) Direct precedent in the SAME FILE: the profile.languages[*].loc description already records WI-bozid removing the phantom 'lines'/'percentage' keys the producer never emitted — identical defect, identical remedy, already applied once here. (2) Populating them would mint a SECOND home for a derivable fact: per-language counts already live in profile.languages[*].{files, loc} and repo-wide counts in metrics. That is exactly the duplicate home the WI-palon ruling declined for profile.loc vs node.line_span.\n\nNo SCHEMA_VERSION bump: removing an optional property that nothing ever emitted changes no artifact and no validation outcome (INV-padoz precedent, where deleting an EMITTED field also did not bump)."  # e98c
